    item-133 at level 2: text: [t]0.5
    item-134 at level 2: text: Multi-Head Attention
    item-135 at level 2: picture
    item-136 at level 2: caption: (left) Scaled Dot-Product Attent ...  attention layers running in parallel.
  item-137 at level 1: text: 
    item-138 at level 2: inline: group group
      item-139 at level 3: text: Instead of performing a single attention function with 
      item-140 at level 3: formula: d_{\text{model}}
      item-141 at level 3: text: -dimensional keys, values and qu ...  project the queries, keys and values 
      item-142 at level 3: formula: h
      item-143 at level 3: text:  times with different, learned linear projections to 
      item-144 at level 3: formula: d_k
      item-145 at level 3: text: , 
      item-146 at level 3: formula: d_k
      item-147 at level 3: text:  and 
      item-148 at level 3: formula: d_v
      item-149 at level 3: text:  dimensions, respectively. On ea ... ention function in parallel, yielding 
      item-150 at level 3: formula: d_v
      item-151 at level 3: text: -dimensional output values. Thes ... epicted in Figure[fig:multi-head-att].
  item-152 at level 1: paragraph: Multi-head attention allows the  ... tention head, averaging inhibits this.
  item-153 at level 1: formula: \begin{align*}
    \mathrm{Multi ... QW^Q_i, KW^K_i, VW^V_i)\\
\end{align*}
  item-154 at level 1: text: 
    item-155 at level 2: inline: group group
      item-156 at level 3: text: Where the projections are parameter matrices 
      item-157 at level 3: formula: W^Q_i \in \mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{model}} \times d_k}
      item-158 at level 3: text: , 
      item-159 at level 3: formula: W^K_i \in \mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{model}} \times d_k}
      item-160 at level 3: text: , 
      item-161 at level 3: formula: W^V_i \in \mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{model}} \times d_v}
      item-162 at level 3: text:  and 
      item-163 at level 3: formula: W^O \in \mathbb{R}^{hd_v \times d_{\text{model}}}
      item-164 at level 3: text: .
  item-165 at level 1: text: 
    item-166 at level 2: inline: group group
      item-167 at level 3: text: In this work we employ 
      item-168 at level 3: formula: h=8
      item-169 at level 3: text:  parallel attention layers, or heads. For each of these we use 
      item-170 at level 3: formula: d_k=d_v=d_{\text{model}}/h=64
      item-171 at level 3: text: . Due to the reduced dimension o ... ad attention with full dimensionality.
  item-172 at level 1: section_header: Applications of Attention in our Model
  item-173 at level 1: text: The Transformer uses multi-head attention in three different ways:
  item-174 at level 1: list: group list
    item-175 at level 2: list_item: In "encoder-decoder attention" l ...  bahdanau2014neural,JonasFaceNet2017].
    item-176 at level 2: list_item: The encoder contains self-attent ...  in the previous layer of the encoder.
    item-177 at level 2: list_item: 
      item-178 at level 3: inline: group group
        item-179 at level 4: text: Similarly, self-attention layers ...  attention by masking out (setting to 
        item-180 at level 4: formula: -\infty
        item-181 at level 4: text: ) all values in the input of the ... ions.  See Figure[fig:multi-head-att].
  item-182 at level 1: section_header: Position-wise Feed-Forward Networks
  item-183 at level 1: paragraph: In addition to attention sub-lay ... ons with a ReLU activation in between.
  item-184 at level 1: formula: \begin{equation}
   \mathrm{FFN} ... , xW_1 + b_1) W_2 + b_2
\end{equation}
  item-185 at level 1: text: 
    item-186 at level 2: inline: group group
      item-187 at level 3: text: While the linear transformations ... dimensionality of input and output is 
      item-188 at level 3: formula: d_{\text{model}}=512
      item-189 at level 3: text: , and the inner-layer has dimensionality 
      item-190 at level 3: formula: d_{ff}=2048
      item-191 at level 3: text: .
  item-192 at level 1: section_header: Embeddings and Softmax
  item-193 at level 1: text: 
    item-194 at level 2: inline: group group
      item-195 at level 3: text: Similarly to other sequence tran ... output tokens to vectors of dimension 
      item-196 at level 3: formula: d_{\text{model}}
      item-197 at level 3: text: .  We also use the usual learned ...  layers, we multiply those weights by 
      item-198 at level 3: formula: \sqrt{d_{\text{model}}}
      item-199 at level 3: text: .
  item-200 at level 1: section_header: Positional Encoding
  item-201 at level 1: text: 
    item-202 at level 2: inline: group group
      item-203 at level 3: text: Since our model contains no recu ... nal encodings have the same dimension 
      item-204 at level 3: formula: d_{\text{model}}
      item-205 at level 3: text:  as the embeddings, so that the  ...  learned and fixed [JonasFaceNet2017].
  item-206 at level 1: paragraph: In this work, we use sine and cosine functions of different frequencies:
  item-207 at level 1: formula: \begin{align*}
    PE_{(pos,2i)} ... 00^{2i/d_{\text{model}}})
\end{align*}
  item-208 at level 1: text: 
    item-209 at level 2: inline: group group
      item-210 at level 3: text: where 
      item-211 at level 3: formula: pos
      item-212 at level 3: text:  is the position and 
      item-213 at level 3: formula: i
      item-214 at level 3: text:  is the dimension.  That is, eac ... ths form a geometric progression from 
      item-215 at level 3: formula: 2\pi
      item-216 at level 3: text:  to 
      item-217 at level 3: formula: 10000 \cdot 2\pi
      item-218 at level 3: text: .  We chose this function becaus ... positions, since for any fixed offset 
      item-219 at level 3: formula: k
      item-220 at level 3: text: , 
      item-221 at level 3: formula: PE_{pos+k}
      item-222 at level 3: text:  can be represented as a linear function of 
      item-223 at level 3: formula: PE_{pos}
      item-224 at level 3: text: .
  item-225 at level 1: text: We also experimented with using  ...  the ones encountered during training.
  item-226 at level 1: section_header: Why Self-Attention
  item-227 at level 1: text: 
    item-228 at level 2: inline: group group
      item-229 at level 3: text: In this section we compare vario ... th sequence of symbol representations 
      item-230 at level 3: formula: (x_1, ..., x_n)
      item-231 at level 3: text:  to another sequence of equal length 
      item-232 at level 3: formula: (z_1, ..., z_n)
      item-233 at level 3: text: , with 
      item-234 at level 3: formula: x_i, z_i \in \mathbb{R}^d
      item-235 at level 3: text: , such as a hidden layer in a ty ... ttention we consider three desiderata.
  item-236 at level 1: paragraph: One is the total computational c ... ber of sequential operations required.
  item-237 at level 1: text: The third is the path length bet ... composed of the different layer types.
  item-238 at level 1: caption: 
    item-239 at level 2: inline: group group
      item-240 at level 3: text: Maximum path lengths, per-layer  ... operations for different layer types. 
      item-241 at level 3: formula: n
      item-242 at level 3: text:  is the sequence length, 
      item-243 at level 3: formula: d
      item-244 at level 3: text:  is the representation dimension, 
      item-245 at level 3: formula: k
      item-246 at level 3: text:  is the kernel size of convolutions and 
      item-247 at level 3: formula: r
      item-248 at level 3: text:  the size of the neighborhood in restricted self-attention.
  item-249 at level 1: table with [7x4]
    item-249 at level 2: caption: 
    item-250 at level 2: unspecified: group group
      item-251 at level 3: text: 
        item-252 at level 4: inline: group group
