  item-298 at level 1: text: 
    item-299 at level 2: inline: group group
      item-300 at level 3: text: As noted in Table [tab:op_comple ... s, whereas a recurrent layer requires 
      item-301 at level 3: formula: O(n)
      item-302 at level 3: text:  sequential operations. In terms ... rrent layers when the sequence length 
      item-303 at level 3: formula: n
      item-304 at level 3: text:  is smaller than the representation dimensionality 
      item-305 at level 3: formula: d
      item-306 at level 3: text: , which is most often the case w ... nsidering only a neighborhood of size 
      item-307 at level 3: formula: r
      item-308 at level 3: text:  in the input sequence centered  ... d increase the maximum path length to 
      item-309 at level 3: formula: O(n/r)
      item-310 at level 3: text: . We plan to investigate this approach further in future work.
  item-311 at level 1: text: 
    item-312 at level 2: inline: group group
      item-313 at level 3: text: A single convolutional layer with kernel width 
      item-314 at level 3: formula: k < n
      item-315 at level 3: text:  does not connect all pairs of i ... sitions. Doing so requires a stack of 
      item-316 at level 3: formula: O(n/k)
      item-317 at level 3: text:  convolutional layers in the case of contiguous kernels, or 
      item-318 at level 3: formula: O(log_k(n))
      item-319 at level 3: text:  in the case of dilated convolut ... than recurrent layers, by a factor of 
      item-320 at level 3: formula: k
      item-321 at level 3: text: . Separable convolutions [xcepti ... rease the complexity considerably, to 
      item-322 at level 3: formula: O(k \cdot n \cdot d + n \cdot d^2)
      item-323 at level 3: text: . Even with 
      item-324 at level 3: formula: k=n
      item-325 at level 3: text: , however, the complexity of a s ... er, the approach we take in our model.
  item-326 at level 1: paragraph: As side benefit, self-attention  ... d semantic structure of the sentences.
  item-327 at level 1: section_header: Training
  item-328 at level 1: text: This section describes the training regime for our models.
  item-329 at level 1: section_header: Training Data and Batching
  item-330 at level 1: text: We trained on the standard WMT 2 ... source tokens and 25000 target tokens.
  item-331 at level 1: section_header: Hardware and Schedule
  item-332 at level 1: text: We trained our models on one mac ...  trained for 300,000 steps (3.5 days).
  item-333 at level 1: section_header: Optimizer
  item-334 at level 1: text: 
    item-335 at level 2: inline: group group
      item-336 at level 3: text: We used the Adam optimizer[kingma2014adam] with 
      item-337 at level 3: formula: \beta_1=0.9
      item-338 at level 3: text: , 
      item-339 at level 3: formula: \beta_2=0.98
      item-340 at level 3: text:  and 
      item-341 at level 3: formula: \epsilon=10^{-9}
      item-342 at level 3: text: .  We varied the learning rate o ... of training, according to the formula:
  item-343 at level 1: formula: \begin{equation}
lrate = d_{\tex ... {warmup\_steps}^{-1.5})
\end{equation}
  item-344 at level 1: text: 
    item-345 at level 2: inline: group group
      item-346 at level 3: text: This corresponds to increasing the learning rate linearly for the first 
      item-347 at level 3: formula: warmup\_steps
      item-348 at level 3: text:  training steps, and decreasing  ... are root of the step number.  We used 
      item-349 at level 3: formula: warmup\_steps=4000
      item-350 at level 3: text: .
  item-351 at level 1: section_header: Regularization
  item-352 at level 1: text: We employ three types of regularization during training:
  item-353 at level 1: text: 
    item-354 at level 2: inline: group group
      item-355 at level 3: text: Residual Dropout We apply dropou ...  For the base model, we use a rate of 
      item-356 at level 3: formula: P_{drop}=0.1
      item-357 at level 3: text: .
  item-358 at level 1: text: 
    item-359 at level 2: inline: group group
      item-360 at level 3: text: Label Smoothing During training, we employed label smoothing of value 
      item-361 at level 3: formula: \epsilon_{ls}=0.1
      item-362 at level 3: text:  [DBLP:journals/corr/SzegedyVISW ...  but improves accuracy and BLEU score.
